  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CFC Phase-out Management Plan for Antigua and Barbuda</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The National CFC Phase-Out Management Plan for Antigua and Barbuda will assist the country in phasing out its  remaining CFC consumption (Annex A, Group 1 chemicals) and meet its obligations under the Montreal Protocol on Substances that deplete the Ozone Layer. To achieve this end, the main focus will be on reducing the demand of CFC for servicing of remaining CFC-based refrigeration equipment. Specific tasks will include: - Studying CFC use in concerned subsectors - Providing training to refrigeration technicians in good management practices - Encouraging affordable retrofit of remaining CFC equipment as a component in the training program and encourage service providers to develop and implement such retrofits - Providing training to customs officials to support the Government&apos;s quota system - Providing funding to cover the incremental cost of retrofits and/or conversions in the food market and mini market refrigeration area that eliminate CFC as refrigerant.</narrative>
  </description>
